    "topic": "Adjuvant",
    "trials": [],
    "answer": "B",
    "explanation": "(A)HER2 positive: HER2 3+ or HER 2+& HER2 FISH positive (defined as an\naverage of >6 HER2 gene copies/nucleus for test systems without an internal\ncontrol probe or HER2/CEP 17 ratio of more than 2.2)\n(B) NSABP B-31/ NCCTG N9831 中比較 Trastuzumab + adjuvant\nchemotherapy, 8 yrs follow-up: Trastuzumab+ chemo significantly prolong OS\n(10 yr OS 84% vs 75.2%; HR 0.63, p<0.001)及\nDFS (10 yrs DFS 73.7% vs 62.2%, HR 0.6, p<0.001);\n但是收案為 at least cT1c(>1cm) or N+,題幹為大於 5mm\nref: N Engl J Med 2005; 353:1673-1684\n(C) BCIRG-006 trial 欲探討 adjuvant TCH 的 efficacy 及 safety; 結果\n發現 TCH 的 efficacy 與傳統 AC-TH 相當,且產生較少的心臟毒性\n((P<0.001)及 leukemia。\nref: N Engl J Med 2011; 365:1273-1283\n(D) 根據 APHINITY trial,adjuvant pertuzumab+標準 trastuzumab 併\nchemotherapy 可以改善 1.6% DFS(7.1% vs 8.7%, HR 0.81, p=0.045); 雖然\nsubgroup analysis LN(-) no benefit; 但是此 trial 收 node positive 或是 node\nnegative 但 T>1cm,為一個 positive trial,且題幹為”可以考慮”\nref: N Engl J Med 2017; 377:122-131\n(E) 根據 ExteNET trial,若病人完成 adjuvant trastuzumab 併 chemotherapy\n後,再加吃 1 年的 pan-HER inhibitor neratinib,可以再增加 2.3%的 2yr\ninvasive DFS(HR 0.67, 95% CI 0.50-0.91; p=0.0091);次族群分析裡,發\n現 HR-positive 病人相較 HR-negative 獲益較大。\nref: Lancet Oncol. 2016 Mar;17(3):367-377",
