    "explanation": "Which of the following statements about molecular testing for\nhepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) is wrong?\n(A) 對 (ref. HCC NCCN V2 2023 HCC-H):\n(B) 對 (ref. HCC NCCN V2 2023 MS-38): There is no established\nindication for routine molecular profiling in HCC. Tumor molecular\ntesting may be warranted in patients with atypical histology, combined\nHCC-CCA histology, or unusual clinical presentations. Evidence\nremains insufficient for definitive recommendations regarding specific\ncriteria to guide genetic risk assessment in hepatobiliary cancers or for\nuniversal germline testing in these tumors.\n(C) 錯。ICI 在 HCC 有被建議使用,但是 All-comer 方式建議而不是綁定\nbiomarkers. (ref. HCC NCCN V2 2023 HCC-H):\n(D) 對,雖然選項有點武斷,但 NCCN V2 2023 HCC-H 確實是這樣寫的\n(ref. HCC NCCN V2 2023 MS-38): There is no established indication for\nroutine molecular profiling in HCC. Tumor molecular testing may be warranted in patients with atypical histology, combined HCC-CCA\nhistology, or unusual clinical presentations. Evidence remains\ninsufficient for definitive recommendations regarding specific criteria to\nguide genetic risk assessment in hepatobiliary cancers or for universal\ngermline testing in these tumors.\n(E) 對 (ref. HCC NCCN V2 2023 HCC-G): 可以看到 Atezolizumab +\nBevacizumab 跟 Tremelimumab-actl + Durvalumab 都是 category 1.",
