    "id": "112-Q052",
    "stem": "Which description about the operation for pancreatic adenocarcinoma is correct?",
    "options": {
      "A": "Tumor contacting with superior mesenteric vein (SMV) £ 180o is called borderline resectable.",
      "B": "Tumor with size larger than 6 cm and stomach invasion is called unresectable.",
      "C": "Around 30% of patients who have operable pancreatic cancer in image will turn out to have metastatic lesions during operation.",
      "D": "The benefit of preoperational chemotherapy is greatest for those who have borderline resectable tumor.",
      "E": "Because the advance of chemotherapy, we should suggest neoadjuvant chemotherapy for patients who have pancreatic tumor with size 1.5 cm."
    },
    "sourcePage": null,
    "cancer": "GI",
    "topic": "Neoadjuvant",
    "trials": [],
    "answer": "C",
    "explanation": "Which description about the operation for pancreatic adenocarcinoma is\ncorrect?\n***這題有點難,因為其實 NCCN 給的建議都有討論空間,話都沒有說\n死,所以有點難直接判斷對錯,但 C 選項的數據是查的到的,而有關其\n他選項 NCCN 在 INTRO 就直接開宗明義說任何決定都須 MDT 討論 (ref.\nNCCN Pancreatic adenocarcinoma V1 2024 INTRO):\nDecisions about diagnostic management and resectability should\ninvolve multidisciplinary consultation at a high-volume center with use of\nappropriate imaging studies.\n(A) 錯。SMV 接觸面≤180’ NCCN 定義上可能是 Resectable disease 也\n可能是 borderline resectable,真正關鍵是有無 Venous contour\nirregularity (ref. NCCN Pancreatic adenocarcinoma V1 2024 Devita 中也有寫到,SMV 接觸面<180 度為 Resectable;接觸面>180 度\n才是 Borderline resectable。\n(Ref. Devita, Practice of Oncology, 12e, p.518)\n(B) 錯(可能有爭議)。NCCN 本身沒有特別定義 Unresectable disease,而是\n定義 locally advanced disease。而 locally advanced disease 也跟胃侵犯和大\n小無關 (ref. NCCN Pancreatic adenocarcinoma V1 2024 PANC-C,同\n上)。\n另外(ref. Pancreatic adenocarcinoma NCCN V1 2024 MS-34): The panel has\nadapted the criteria put forth by other groups and lists its recommended\ncriteria for defining resectability status in the guidelines. The consensus of the panel is that patients should be selected for surgery on the basis\nof curative intent as determined by the probability of obtaining negative\n(R0) resection margins. Overall, the likelihood of attaining negative\nmargins is the key criterion for consideration when determining whether\na patient is a potential candidate for resection。\nAlthough it is clear that patients with visceral, peritoneal, or pleural metastases\nor with metastases to nodes beyond the field of resection derive no benefit from\nresection, institutions differ in their approaches to patients with locoregional\ndisease\ninvolvement (pancreas and peripancreatic lymph nodes) (ref. pancreatic\nadenocarcinoma NCCN V1 2024 MS-33).\n而 NCCN 有引用到一篇期刊有使用 unresectable disease 這個名詞(Ann Surg\nOncol (2012) 19:1663–1669)。 在這篇期刊的研究方式中有提出 locally\nunresectable 胰臟癌的定義,為 Stage III disease。NCCN Stage III 胰臟癌的\n分期方式為: 如果是用 Stage III 以上定義 unresectable disease,確實吃到胃應該可以稱\n之 unresectable,但是這篇論文的定義方式並沒有廣泛共識,至少沒被寫\n在 NCCN guideline 中,所以如果從 NCCN 的角度來看應該是只有 locally\nadvanced disease 這名詞。偏錯但是可能有爭議,畢竟一些期刊 Stage III 以\n上稱為 unresectable。\n(C) 對。If a person is said to have resectable disease after diagnostic\nlaparoscopy and CT scan, there is a 20% probability that their cancer\nwill be unresectable compared to a 41% probability for those receiving\nCT alone (Cochrane Database Syst Rev. 2016 Jul 6;7(7):CD009323.) 影像學判斷可開後上刀發現不可開的機率是 40%;影像學加上診斷性腹\n腔鏡判斷可開後上刀發現不可開的機率是 20%,Cochrane 的 data 其實\n大約 30%上下。\n(D) 錯。(ref. Pancreatic adenocarcinoma NCCN V1 2024 MS-46):\nPatients with borderline resectable disease should be considered for\nneoadjuvant therapy, followed by restaging and resection in patients\nwithout disease progression precluding surgery. The use of neoadjuvant\ntherapy in the setting of borderline resectable disease has been a highly\ndebated topic. However, although there is no high-level evidence\nsupporting its use, most NCCN Member Institutions now prefer an initial\napproach involving neoadjuvant therapy, as opposed to immediate\nsurgery, for patients with borderline resectable disease. If neoadjuvant\ntherapy is recommended, treatment should preferably be administered\nat or coordinated through a high-volume center, when feasible. Upfront\nresection in patients with borderline resectable disease is no longer\nrecommended, as of the 2016 version of these guidelines.\n照 NCCN 以上的描述,borderline resectable disease 的 neoadjuvant 是\npreferred 大於直接開刀,但實質上這議題是具爭議,並且沒有高度證據\n支持的,所以這現狀跟選項中提出的 Neoadjuvant 最具效益族群有偏\n差。但確實是有幾篇期刊是支持 neoadjuvant 在 borderline resectable\ndisease 的角色,包括: Cancer Invest. 2007 Jun;25(4):267-73.\n(E) 錯。Neoadjuvant 要不要打,以 NCCN 來說還是要看 resectability,\n而不是單純腫瘤大小。而就連 resectable disease,目前 NCCN 給\nneoadjuvant 的建議是都可以 (ref. NCCN V1 2024 PANC-2):所以答案看起來是尚無定論,需 MDT case-by-case,而不是單純 1.5cm\n就打 neoadjuvant。況且這選項沒寫 pancreatic tumor 是哪種 tumor,可\n能還需先確認病理化驗才能進一步討論。",
