    "id": "112-Q064",
    "stem": "San-Miguel J, et al. Cilta-cel or Standard Care in Lenalidomide-Refractory Multiple Myeloma. N Engl J Med 389:335-47, 2023 是一個比較cilta-cel 和standard care 的superiority randomized controlled trial，病患藉由電腦產生的碼隨機分派(randomization)至接受standard care 治療 或單次cilta-cel 輸注。Randomization 的stratification(分層)因子包括standard care 的處方 (PVd vs. DPd)、ISS 病情嚴重程度(I vs. II vs. III)、多少種先前治療 (1 vs. 2 至3)。 關於randomization、stratification，下列敘述何者是錯誤的？",
    "options": {
      "A": "Randomization 通常是1 : 1 分配以增加效率。",
      "B": "Randomization 應在簽署同意書之前，randomization 理想中最好愈接近治療開始的時間愈好。",
      "C": "Stratification 可以確保治療組、對照組大致上一樣比例的病患有較好(或壞)的預後因子。",
      "D": "如果stratification 不包括在randomization 之中，也可以做stratified analysis。",
      "E": "Stratification 在小規模的隨機分派臨床試驗相較於大規模的隨機分派臨床試驗更為重要。"
    },
    "sourcePage": null,
    "cancer": "Heme",
    "topic": "Trial interpretation",
    "trials": [],
    "answer": "B",
    "explanation": "(A) 正確。\nSimple or unrestricted, equal randomization of patients between 2 treatment\ngroups is equivalent to tossing a fair coin for each patient assignment.\n(B) 錯誤。會先簽完同意書,確認要參加試驗,才會抽籤分組\n(C) 正確。\nResearchers hope to balance the prognostic factors between the study\ngroups, but randomization does not eliminate all the imbalances in prognostic\nfactors\n\n(D) 正確。Trial 裡面常出現的 subgroup analysis 就是 randomization 後才做的\nstratified analysis,因為不在一開始的研究設計裡,所以評讀上很常會因\npower 不足,只能說有沒有 numerical difference\n(E) 正確。\nRestricted randomization procedures such as stratified randomization and\npermuted block randomization create a balance between important\nprognostic characteristics and are useful when conducting randomized trials\nenrolling relatively few patients",
