    "id": "112-Q065",
    "stem": "關於癌症臨床試驗滿足點(endpoint)，下列何者是錯誤的？",
    "options": {
      "A": "以overall survival 為主要滿足點，如果對照組效果很好，會導致試驗規模很大、追蹤 時間很長。",
      "B": "以overall survival 為主要滿足點，如果實驗組、對照組不能crossover，會看不出2 組 overall survival 的差別。",
      "C": "以overall survival 為主要滿足點，如果有competing mortality(例如：輔助性化學治療 用於年紀大病患的臨床試驗)，會稀釋實驗組的治療效果，可以考慮從分析overall survival、 改成分析disease-specific survival。",
      "D": "以progression-free survival 為主要滿足點，如果試驗是unblinded，一個可能的bias 是 assessment time bias。",
      "E": "以progression-free survival 為主要滿足點，如果試驗是unblinded，可以考慮blinded independent central review。"
    },
    "sourcePage": null,
    "cancer": "Heme",
    "topic": "Adjuvant",
    "trials": [],
    "answer": "B",
    "explanation": "詳解:\n根據 Lancet Oncol 2015; 16: e32–42\n(A)、(B) 正確。overall survival 病人數多,crossover 反而才會影響 survival 結果\n\n(C)正確。J Natl Cancer Inst Monogr 2014;49:145–186\nRelative survival is the preferred method to compare survival between different\nregistries and across countries because the cause of death may not be available\nor there may be variability in the accurate determination of cause of death across\ncountries. When cancer patients differ considerably from the general population\nconcerning important personal factors, which may affect deaths from other\ncauses (such as socio-economic status, health status, and health behaviors like\nsmoking), relative survival can be biased.\n(D) 正確。J Clin Oncol 25:2122-2126\nA potential problem with PFS, however, occurs when the patients and\ninvestigators are not blinded to the treatment assignment. There are two\npossible explanations for this differential reporting of events (assessment or\nevaluation bias)\n(E) 正確。J Clin Oncol 26:3791-3796\nThe potential for subjective elements to affect end-point assessment\ndifferentially across treatment arms leads to concerns about biased\nevaluation, particularly in unblinded trials. Blinded independent central review\n(BICR) is one strategy proposed to reduce the potential for this bias.",
