    "answer": "C",
    "explanation": "詳解:\n先了解 Umbrella trial:單一疾病找 target gene;Basket trial:多數疾病表現單一\ntarget gene\n(A) 正確。\n“Lung-MAP is a unique public-private partnership that has increased the\naccess to new treatment options for patients with lung cancer across the\ncountry”→single disease for multiple targets\n(B) 正確。\nThe ground-breaking I-SPY 2 trial of neoadjuvant treatment for locally\nadvanced breast cancer established a new benchmark for the efficiency of\n\nphase II clinical trials. I-SPY 2 was one of the first, and is now the longest-\nrunning 'platform' trial ever. As a platform trial, I-SPY 2 uses a master\n\nprotocol that provides a regulatory framework to study multiple treatments in\nthe same study. →single disease for multiple targets\n(C) 錯誤。為 Umbrella trial\nPatients with advanced NSCLC (excluding sensitizing EGFR mutations and\nALK gene fusions) refractory to more than one prior therapy were randomly\nassigned, stratified by KRAS status, to four arms: (1) erlotinib, (2) erlotinib\nplus MK-2206, (3) MK-2206 plus AZD6244, or (4) sorafenib. Tumor gene\nexpression profiling–targeted next-generation sequencing was performed to evaluate predictive and prognostic biomarkers. →single disease for multiple\ntargets\n(D) 正確。\nNCI-MATCH, also known as MATCH, is a precision medicine cancer\ntreatment clinical trial that sought to find out if treating cancer based on\nspecific genetic changes in a person’s tumor is effective, no matter the cancer\ntype. → single target for multiple diseases\n(E) 正確。\nWe included adult patients with any kind of metastatic solid tumor refractory\nto standard of care. We only included patients for whom a molecular\nalteration was identified within one of three molecular pathways (hormone\nreceptor, PI3K/AKT/mTOR, RAF/MEK) → single target for multiple diseases",
