    "stem": "About bone targeting agents in the treatment of prostate cancer, the following statements are correct: (1) Use of Radium-223 in mCRPC with bone metastasis by Phase III ALSYMPCA Trial (2) The addition of radium-223 to abiraterone may improve symptomatic skeletal event-free survival in patients with castration-resistant prostate cancer and bone metastases by ERA-223 trial. (3) Adding bone-protecting agents may decrease the incidence of fracture in combination use of Ra-223 and enzalutamide by PEACE-3 trial. (4) Lu-PSMA-617 can be used to treat all types of bone metastasis CRPC by vision trial.",
