    "topic": "Other",
    "trials": [],
    "answer": "E",
    "explanation": "All four options are correct contributing factors to anemia in cancer patients. The pathogenesis of cancer-related anemia is multifactorial, involving:\n\nChemotherapy - Direct myelosuppression of erythroid precursors (60-90% of patients receiving chemotherapy) \n[1-2]\n\nTumor bleeding - Acute or chronic blood loss causing iron deficiency anemia \n[2][4-5][9]\n\nMalnutrition - Deficiencies in iron, folate, vitamin B12, and protein-calorie malnutrition \n[1-2][5-6][10]\n\nCancer-related cytokines - IL-6, TNF-α, IL-1, and IFN-γ causing functional iron deficiency, suppressed erythropoiesis, impaired erythropoietin production, and shortened RBC lifespan",
